Your storefront's own static files go in this directory — a logo, an og-image, a favicon you own.

They are served at `/assets/<name>`, and that address is load-bearing in two places you would otherwise
have to discover: the Dockerfile next to this tree COPYies `public/`, and `src/middleware.ts` excludes
`assets/` from host->store rewriting. A file dropped at the ROOT of `public/` instead gets rewritten into
the store tree and 404s, with the file sitting in the image the whole time.

This placeholder only keeps the directory in git. Delete it once you have put something real here.
